From a943c1c8ad7ea9f18501e8c3dfc61d2737091552 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 23:45:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] [feature](be) Add snapshot-remote-unwind signal handler
 infrastructure

Mirrors OceanBase's MP_SIG dispatch + two-phase per-thread coordination
under a separate symbol set (kMpSig / g_sig_handler_ctx_ /
srunwind_signal_handler) so the variant branch stays self-contained
relative to Phase C's ob-kill60 series.

The defining divergence from ob-kill60: the worker handler does NO
libunwind work. It captures the ucontext_t verbatim and memcpy's up to
kMaxSnapshotStackBytes (8 KiB per docs/phase2-plan.md:99) starting at
%rsp into a fixed shared buffer; the coordinator runs libunwind remote
unwind against the snapshot. Stack copy uses process_vm_readv (an
async-signal-safe Linux syscall) so a bad %rsp returns -1 instead of
faulting inside the handler. Stack-VMA bounds clamp the read so it
never crosses a guard page even if the kernel just grew the stack.

Anti-spoof req_id check and target_tid check identical to ob-kill60.
install_srunwind_signal_handler narrows to MP_SIG only so it coexists
with Doris's existing InstallFailureSignalHandler.

Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_struct.h:111-127
Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_struct.cpp:90-110
Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_handlers.cpp:73-120
Reference: docs/phase2-plan.md:67-71,99
---
